<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal, oil down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained bearish in central Indian markets and fell by 800-1,000 rupees per tonne on Wednesday. Demand from processing plants was limited. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices also remained bearish and fell by 300 rupees per tonne. Demand was very poor in thin trading. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were also bearish. Soymeal yellow was down by $10 and rapeseed extraction was down by $3-4 per tonne. Soymeal yellow was $245-247 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $92-96 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
